Keep a shared tokens as an empty list of text.
Keep a shared token as empty text.
Keep a shared nextspot as 0.
Keep a shared atom as empty text.
Keep a shared wanted as empty text.
Keep a shared parsevalue as 0.
Keep a shared numbervalue as 0.
Keep a shared lookupvalue as 0.
Keep a shared depth as 0.
Keep a shared groupclose as 0.
Keep a shared names as an empty list of text.
Keep a shared values as an empty list of whole numbers.
To flush.
If the length of token is more than 0, Place token into tokens, set token to empty text.

To seekclose from spot (a whole number).
If spot is more than the last position of tokens, return.
The piece is item spot of tokens.
If piece matches "(", add 1 to depth.
If piece matches ")", subtract 1 from depth.
If depth is 0, set groupclose to spot, return.
Seekclose from spot plus 1.

To shrink from base (a whole number).
If the last position of names is less than base, return.
remove the last item from names.
remove the last item from values.
Shrink from base.

To lookup from spot (a whole number).
If spot is less than 0, return.
If item spot of names matches wanted, set lookupvalue to item spot of values, return.
Lookup from spot minus 1.

To numbervalue from spot (a whole number).
If spot is more than the last position of atom, return.
The letter is character spot of atom.
The digit is the digit value of letter.
Set numbervalue to numbervalue times 10 plus digit.
Numbervalue from spot plus 1.

To parsenumber.
Set numbervalue to 0.
Numbervalue from 0.
Set parsevalue to numbervalue.
Add 1 to nextspot.

To parse.
The spot is nextspot.
Set atom to item spot of tokens.
If atom matches "(", parselist, return.
If atom matches ")", return.
The firstchar is character 0 of atom.
If firstchar is between "0" and "9", parsenumber, return.
Set wanted to atom.
The top is the last position of names.
Lookup from top.
Set parsevalue to lookupvalue.
Add 1 to nextspot.

To parselist.
Add 1 to nextspot.
The spot is nextspot.
The operator is item spot of tokens.
Add 1 to nextspot.
If operator matches "add", parseadd, return.
If operator matches "mult", parsemult, return.
If operator matches "let", parselet, return.

To parseadd.
Parse.
The first is parsevalue.
Parse.
The second is parsevalue.
Add 1 to nextspot.
Set parsevalue to first plus second.

To parsemult.
Parse.
The first is parsevalue.
Parse.
The second is parsevalue.
Add 1 to nextspot.
Set parsevalue to first times second.

To parselet.
Set depth to 0.
The open is nextspot minus 2.
Seekclose from open.
The top is the last position of names.
The base is top plus 1.
The finish is groupclose.
Letpairs with base and finish.

To finishlet with base (a whole number).
Parse.
Shrink from base.

To letpairs with base (a whole number) and finish (a whole number).
The spot is nextspot.
The atom is item spot of tokens.
If atom matches "(", Finishlet with base, return.
If nextspot plus 1 is finish, Finishlet with base, return.
The name is atom.
Add 1 to nextspot.
Parse.
Place name into names.
Place parsevalue into values.
Letpairs with base and finish.

The expression is "(let x 2 (mult x (let x 3 y 4 (add x y))))".
The last is the last position of expression.
For every spot from 0 to last.
The symbol is the slice of expression from spot to spot plus 1.
The special is 0.
The brace is 0.
If symbol matches "(", set brace to 1, set special to 1.
If symbol matches ")", set brace to 1, set special to 1.
If symbol matches " ", set special to 1.
If special is 1, Flush.
If special is 0, Place symbol into token.
If brace is 1, Place symbol into tokens.

Flush.
Set nextspot to 0.
Parse.
Show parsevalue.
